course: dictionary
lesson: 5929
title: Animals with pouches
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A marsupial is a mammal whose babies are born very small and then grow inside a pouch on the mother's body. A mammal is an animal that feeds its babies milk, and a marsupial is one special kind of mammal. «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» The pouch is the clue: it is a bag on the mother's body where the baby stays and grows.
explain: Marsupial can be a noun or an adjective. «A marsupial» names an animal, but «marsupial animals» describes animals of that kind. Look at the words around it to tell which one it is.
explain: Context also helps you avoid wrong ideas. «The thylacine, or Tasmanian tiger, was a striped meat-eating marsupial that looked like a dog.» The clues are striped and meat-eating, so not every marsupial is a cuddly, plant-eating animal. Read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: A marsupial is a mammal whose babies grow inside a pouch.
fact: Kangaroos, koalas, wombats, possums and Tasmanian devils are marsupials.
fact: Most marsupials live in Australia and New Guinea; the opossum lives in the Americas.
fact: A baby kangaroo or koala is called a joey.
fact: «The red kangaroo is the largest marsupial» and can hop at over fifty kilometres an hour.
exercise: «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» Where do the babies stay? | In a hard shell | *In a pouch on the mother's body | In the water beside the mother | In a nest high up a tree
exercise: What is a joey? | A type of tree | A small fish | A kind of pouch | *A baby kangaroo or koala
exercise: Which animal is a marsupial? | A horse | A dog | *A kangaroo | A lion
test: Which place is home to the opossum? | Australia | Africa | New Guinea | *The Americas
test: In «marsupial animals carry their babies in a pouch», what job does marsupial do? | It is a kind of food | It is a number | It names a place | *It describes the animals
exam: Ben reads «The thylacine was a striped meat-eating marsupial» and says all marsupials are cuddly and eat only plants. What does the text show? | Marsupials are not mammals | All marsupials have stripes | *Some marsupials eat meat, so Ben is wrong | All marsupials live in water
